new file mode 100644
index 0000000..b49fb76
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/bot-webhooks.md
@@ -0,0 +1,36 @@
+# Bot mention callbacks
+
+Bots are ordinary users, so existing room-scoped mention autocomplete and signed mention
+attachments work for bots without a separate frontend implementation. Only active bot members
+of the room receive callbacks; repeated mentions produce one callback per bot per message.
+Literal `@name` text is not a signed mention. Command text removes only the recipient's verified
+mention attachments, preserving other mentions and literal names. The HTML body is the full
+stored rich-text body.
+
+Webhook settings are owner/admin scoped, alongside the bot's name and avatar. The additive
+`chat_bot_webhooks` table allows upgrades of existing Rust and Rails databases without altering
+Rails tables. Empty input deletes the setting; omitted input preserves it. URLs must be absolute
+HTTP(S), without userinfo or fragments. Internal services are intentionally supported, so bot
+managers should be trusted to configure outbound HTTP destinations on the Campfire network.
+
+After a message is committed and broadcast, an in-memory job resolves recipients and sends JSON
+callbacks. Posting never awaits the HTTP call. Delivery uses the existing bounded best-effort
+job runner: no retries, and queued work can be lost on crashes or queue overflow. Within a job,
+up to four recipients run concurrently; failures are isolated per recipient. Each HTTP exchange
+has a 15-second total deadline and replies are limited to 1 MiB. Redirects are never followed,
+since the payload's `room.reply_to` contains the bot's secret posting credential. Do not log
+payloads or share that path with other services.
+
+Only HTTP 200 with `text/plain` or `text/html` posts a nonblank UTF-8 reply. Plain text is escaped;
+HTML uses the normal Action Text pipeline, including sanitization when rendered. HTTP 204, other
+status codes, and unsupported media types produce no message. Replies use normal message
+creation (including search indexing and push events) and room broadcasts. Bot identity, webhook
+configuration, and room membership are checked again before inserting a reply. Bot-authored
+messages never trigger callbacks, avoiding recursive bot-to-bot loops.
+
+The payload contains relative reply and deep-link paths. A bot can return 204 and later post
+literal UTF-8 text to `room.reply_to` using the existing bearer-code API.
+
+Regression command: `cargo test -p campfire bot_webhook`. Tests run a local HTTP service and gate
+its response until after the user's POST returns, exercise the payload and both reply types,
+follow the deep link, post out-of-band, and cover unsupported replies and revocation.
